# Hello Goodbye, verse (figure 120.1)
# Seventeen bars; the C at the end is the downbeat that overlaps with the start of the refrain.
# Pollack's bass notes are kept: F under the d (ii6/5), C under C, G under each V, and in the a
# bars the quarter-note descending scale A G F E D C B A (four to a bar).
# The last phrase is one long G pedal: his figures 13/11 and 5/3 are written C/G and G (he says
# the 13/11 may be called C in 6/4 but he hears G as the root), and 11/9/7 as G11.
# Added: the bass A under the second pair of a bars, the G in the last phrase (his "G as the root
# note throughout") and the C at the end.
#? Bass octaves are a choice (F2, C3, G2; the scale from A3 down to A2): check the register of the scale against the record, which might be an octave lower.
key C

